    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "54a96ac0_6d4bdc8a",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/connectivity/Tethering.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1725,
      "author": {
        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-05T07:45:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Looks to me like you need to lock mPublicSync. Otherwise you might have a remove in the middle of the iteration and NPE or OOB, or an add in the middle of the loop and then miss sending an update to it.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1725,
        "startChar": 27,
        "endLine": 1725,
        "endChar": 51
      },
      "revId": "a77e0cd61eafa73e0e1e72180fc5c37be43639d7",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2f965a18_bf642074",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/connectivity/Tethering.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1730,
      "author": {
        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-05T07:45:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Catching RuntimeException is a code smell. In this case I suspect you are doing this to catch the possible OOB and NPE from removing while iterating, but you also need to account for the add case. Also if you have a call to remove while iterating, you will miss calling one of the callbacks : if e.g. you have four callbacks in the list\n(A, B, C, D)\n\nIterate, call index 1 \u003d A\nIterate, call index 2 \u003d B\nRemove index 1\nIterate, call index 3 \u003d D\nIterate, call index 4, NPE, catch RuntimeException\n\n...you never called C.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1730,
        "startChar": 43,
        "endLine": 1730,
        "endChar": 59
      },
      "revId": "a77e0cd61eafa73e0e1e72180fc5c37be43639d7",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c8f60db4_25e72d3d",
        "filename": "tests/net/java/com/android/server/connectivity/TetheringTest.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 924,
      "author": {
        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-05T07:45:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Instead of a boolean I suggest you have an int, or better yet an array of expected networks. The main reason is to detect duplicated calls. It is also easier to convert later to a semaphore if we want to perform actual thread testing.\n\nA typical way of doing this is to provide an expectations method :\n\n  private final ArrayList\u003cNetwork\u003e expectedUpstreamChanges \u003d new ArrayList\u003c\u003e();\n  public void expectUpstreamChanged(Network... networks) {\n    expectedUpstream.addAll(Arrays.asList(networks));\n  }\n\n  public void onUpstreamChanged(Network network) {\n    assertEquals(network, expectUpstreamChanged.remove(0)) // throws OOB if no expectations\n  }\n\n  public void assertNoCallback() {\n    assertTrue(expectUpstreamChanged.isEmpty());\n  }\n\n\nThen you can use like this :\n\n  listener1.expectUpstreamChanged(upstreamState.network)\n  runUsbTethering(upstreamState);\n  listener1.assertNoCallback();\n\n\nThere are many variations on this depending on your needs and your tastes (for example, you could prefer to throw in expectUpstreamChanged if the array is not empty ; you could have an array of Predicate\u003cNetwork\u003e instead of an array of Network for versatility (and then you could say expectUpstreamChanged(Network::equals) or expectUpstreamChanged({ true }) to accept anything but also other richer expressions) ; you could modify the logic to remember previous calls instead so you can say expect() after the callback has been issued...).\n\nWe are doing something similar in ConnectivityServiceTest#MockNetworkFactory or TestNetworkAgent.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 924,
        "startChar": 15,
        "endLine": 924,
        "endChar": 22
      },
      "revId": "a77e0cd61eafa73e0e1e72180fc5c37be43639d7",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
